From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Vishnefske <jvishnefske@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:42:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] std: cgroup quotas, JoinHandleExt and the stack overflow
 message on linux-none

- thread: available_parallelism caps the affinity count by the cgroup CPU
  quota. Upstream's cgroups module (which only uses fs) moves from
  sys/thread/unix.rs to sys/thread/unix/cgroups.rs, unchanged, so that
  linux_none.rs can include it too.
- os::unix::thread::JoinHandleExt is implemented: the pthread_t is the
  address of linux_none_rt's control block for the thread, and
  into_pthread_t detaches it.
- pal/linux_none/stack_overflow.rs: a SIGSEGV/SIGBUS handler on an
  alternate signal stack (rt's, per thread) that prints "thread '<name>'
  (<tid>) has overflowed its stack" and aborts when the fault is in the
  thread's guard page: rt's for spawned threads, the page below the main
  stack's mapping in /proc/self/maps for the main thread. Other faults get
  the default disposition back.
